      "content": "While staying home, drinking water, and taking prenatal vitamins is a good idea, it's not a replacement for addressing your high blood pressure. Staying hydrated can help alleviate swelling, but a reading of 145/95 is elevated and may indicate a need for monitoring or medication discussion with your doctor, especially at 34 weeks. It's better to relax and take it easy, but also be prepared to discuss your blood pressure with your doctor when you schedule an appointment.",
